  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25 or below) to account for bearish market pressure.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10% to align with historical volatility.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is positive (e.g., +0.50) to counteract overconfidence in upward momentum.",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is below forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 3-5% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Avoid overreacting to single-day sentiment shifts; apply smoothing over 3-5 day windows for sentiment-based adjustments."
